ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"468e7d3474212e185a07c4eb53bec25a1ed0680e96e62c804debe67d29516447","event_uuid":"a1c36ea4-79fc-4e99-a0ae-6912298bc5de","position":{"commit_sha":"3aca30069b59f0f9b7eb28c7d90988c1b184932b","position":"1787897776075435001-a1c36ea4-79fc-4e99-a0ae-6912298bc5de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c874008083ae7a82dd428bf2298dec72343fb0ea6d54e8e1787aeb15ca167629","event_uuid":"ac3bb027-2f5d-4cd1-999c-e1b20bd7506a","position":{"commit_sha":"595427a0ccd4f62c52eef4ae53bab57aefa7b3c9","position":"1787897791143122001-ac3bb027-2f5d-4cd1-999c-e1b20bd7506a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review BLOCK on three findings, all correct.\n\n(1) AC1 named scripts/mutation_sandbox.py as the site of the allow-list construction. Wrong: wrap() RECEIVES allow as a parameter and constructs nothing. The venv-excluding allow-list is built in scripts/mutation_gate.py:execute_shard as sandbox_allow = (root, basetemp), with sys.prefix deliberately absent. AC1 now points at the real authority.\n\n(2 and 3, the same problem) AC3 claimed the fail-open would 'require more than ambient CI alone' while its verification asserted only warning text — a proxy for the requirement, not the requirement. The reviewer noted this left an executor unsure whether to add a real second gate or just improve the message.\n\nDecided rather than fudged: baf9 stays an observability fix, and AC3 now says so explicitly, including that ambient CI REMAINS the sole condition after this ticket. The actual gating change is filed as f11d-f8fd (nubuck-wailsome-bronco, P2), because requiring an explicit opt-in alongside CI is a behaviour change affecting every lane that relies on the fallback and deserves its own review rather than riding along in a docs-and-messages cleanup.","timestamp":1787893089508339001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged as 2311. All four findings addressed:\n\n1. docs/local-dev-env.md said the sandbox permits writes to the venv; the shipped allow-list deliberately EXCLUDES it. Corrected, with the reason stated.\n2. A missing allow-list path was dropped with a bare continue. It now names the path it skipped — silently, a caller who forgot to create a directory saw only a confusing write failure from inside the sandbox with nothing pointing at the cause.\n3. The CI fail-open warning now names the variable AND its observed value. Ambient CI remains the SOLE condition (f11d-f8fd owns tightening it), so the log is the only place a reader can tell a run had no sandbox at all.\n4. docs/mutation-testing.md records what the sandbox does NOT restrict: reads and network are open by design, because write-denial was the hazard and is the scope. Now a decision rather than an accident.\n\nBoth new warnings proven RED by real mutation: removing the missing-path warning failed its test; dropping the CI value from the warning failed its test. Local run 15339 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCI note: patch set 1 failed on ubuntu py3.12 in tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py, unrelated to this change. Root-caused rather than retried blindly: line 642 is a SETUP precondition asserting the ticket blob is stored LOOSE, and rebar deliberately no longer pins gc.auto=0, so an auto gc can pack it and the test fails before exercising anything. Filed as 7bcc-55a9-7a28-412d. py3.11 and py3.13 passed on identical code, the test passed locally four times, and the recheck run was fully green.","timestamp":1787897496863087001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787855640466763001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"012beb23-f96b-4a69-ac5f-b040a48a2547","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"},{"link_uuid":"a990443a-e001-47db-9342-ab0878baab87","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d18e-53e1-ff9e-4079"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nResidual advisory findings from the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 2256 (the\n`e668-b496-e264-4283` mutation sandbox). None blocked the merge; each is a real but\nlower-severity gap. The two higher-severity findings from the same review are tracked\nseparately as `724c-b5fd-efb1-40d5` and `c100-c4f1-2a2b-4905`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Docs contradict the code on the venv.** `docs/local-dev-env.md` describes the\n   sandbox as permitting writes to \"the venv\", but the merged code deliberately\n   EXCLUDES the venv from the allow-list so a mutant cannot write executable code into\n   site-packages. The doc describes a weaker sandbox than the one that shipped; a\n   reader trusting it would mis-model the boundary.\n\n2. **A missing allow path is skipped silently.** `mutation_sandbox` skips a\n   non-existent allow-list path with a bare `continue` rather than surfacing it, because\n   `bwrap --bind` requires SRC to exist. A required path that a future caller fails to\n   create becomes an invisible loss of a writable bind — indistinguishable from an\n   intentionally absent one, and surfacing later as a confusing write failure inside the\n   sandbox.\n\n3. **The CI fail-open keys on an ambient, trivially-set variable** (observability\n   only here; the gate itself is tracked separately — see the criterion). When no mechanism is\n   available and `CI` is truthy, the run proceeds UNSANDBOXED with a warning; on a\n   workstation it aborts. `CI` is inheritable and can be set by anything, so a\n   workstation with `CI=1` exported silently runs mutation tests unsandboxed. The\n   cross-provider `CI` convention is the right portability choice (naming no provider),\n   but it should not be the SOLE gate on the fail-open.\n\n4. **The Seatbelt profile restricts writes only.** `(allow default)` + `(deny\n   file-write*)` leaves reads and network unrestricted, so a mutant under the macOS\n   sandbox can still exfiltrate or read anything the user can. Write-denial was the\n   incident's hazard and is the ticket's scope, but the residual read/network surface\n   should be a recorded decision rather than an accident.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `docs/local-dev-env.md` matches the shipped allow-list: the venv is NOT writable\n      inside the sandbox. Verified against `scripts/mutation_gate.py`, where the\n      allow-list is actually built — `execute_shard` sets `sandbox_allow = (root,\n      basetemp)` with `sys.prefix` deliberately absent. `mutation_sandbox.wrap()` only\n      RECEIVES `allow` as a parameter and constructs nothing.\n- [x] A missing allow-list path is surfaced (log at WARNING naming the path) rather than\n      skipped silently. Verified by a test asserting the warning names the path.\n- [x] The fail-open's WARNING makes the condition unmistakable in the log of any run\n      that took it: it states the run is UNSANDBOXED and names both the variable that\n      permitted it and its observed value. Verified by asserting that text.\n\n      SCOPE, stated so it is not mistaken for the stronger claim: this criterion improves\n      OBSERVABILITY only. It does NOT make the fail-open require more than ambient `CI`,\n      and after this ticket ambient `CI` remains the sole condition. Tightening that gate\n      is a behaviour change affecting every lane that relies on the fallback, so it needs\n      its own review rather than riding along here; tracked as `f11d-f8fd`.\n- [x] The Seatbelt profile's read/network posture is a stated, deliberate decision\n      recorded in `docs/mutation-testing.md`, not an unremarked default.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- Each finding above is either fixed or recorded as a deliberate decision with reasoning.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nDiscovered from `e668-b496-e264-4283`. Source: change 2256 review, patch sets 3-7.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"correct the venv allow-list claim"},{"path":"docs/mutation-testing.md","reason":"record the Seatbelt read/network posture decision"},{"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"surface skipped allow paths; strengthen the fail-open warning"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"tests for the warning texts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d18e-53e1-ff9e-4079"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a1c36ea4-79fc-4e99-a0ae-6912298bc5de","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"baf9-eea0-4b8d-42a4","ticket_type":"task","title":"Residual mutation-sandbox hardening from 2256 review advisories","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["94e36f45-546d-48c7-a5b3-b72eb8703c2e","b5ba739e-e239-4018-880d-4e416e1447d5","b91f3ddf-d318-4b0a-ad41-52b962842660","8c672058-876a-4afe-a97b-c3260703b5f2","99c78868-1748-4449-be20-d4b967e12781","0555b904-36c4-49a4-8533-8b7b7e7a50ae","a990443a-e001-47db-9342-ab0878baab87","c1bf94d1-f304-4c4e-8882-55be483f9786","7508cb5f-b2e8-4e96-b0ba-e74e99754fd8","a1c36ea4-79fc-4e99-a0ae-6912298bc5de","ac3bb027-2f5d-4cd1-999c-e1b20bd7506a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787902387347316001,"uuid":"fa8eee4a-e3bb-4003-b367-ece69c32d3a4"}